data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","output_index":19,"item":{"id":"st_tmp_k04qadnxmm","type":"openrouter:web_fetch","status":"completed","url":"https://www.be-unconditional.com/sugar-was-turning-me-into-a-monster-heres-how-i-broke-free-ep-21/","content":"Sugar Was Turning Me Into A Monster. Here's How I Broke Free | E…\n\nWelcome to UNCONDITIONAL!\n\nFeb. 18, 2026\n\n# Sugar Was Turning Me Into A Monster. Here's How I Broke Free | Ep 21\n\n- Show Notes\n\nThe average American consumes about 17 teaspoons of added sugar per day. It’s in candy and soda, sure… but also pasta sauce, ketchup, and nearly everything processed. At a time when over 70% of adults are overweight or obese—and rates of depression and metabolic disfunction are climbing—it’s worth asking:\n\nIs sugar at the root of the problem?\n\nIn this episode of Unconditional with Norbie Schickel, I share my personal story of how sugar—despite being lean and in shape—was destabilizing my mood, affecting my marriage, and turning me into someone I didn’t like.\n\nWe discuss:\n\n- Metabolic dysfunction, obesity, and insulin resistance\n- The emerging world of metabolic psychiatry\n- Sugar, cancer, and why artificial sweeteners may not be the answer\n- Why willpower is a bad bet\n- Why most substitution strategies fail\n- The two practical shifts that finally helped me break the habit\n\nAnd for the parents out there… how I approach sugar with my own kids.\n\nNo shame. No moralizing. Just effective vs. ineffective—and how to reclaim your health in a world where sugar is everywhere.\n\nIf sugar has its hooks in you… there’s a way out.\n\nCHAPTERS\n\n00:00 The Sugar Epidemic\n\n10:24 Stakes in Context: The Why Behind Sugar's Impact\n\n10:47 The Link Between Sugar, Obesity & Metabolic Health\n\n13:41 Metabolic Psychiatry - The Link Between Sugar & Mental Health\n\n18:32 Sugar, Cancer, and Artificial Sweeteners\n\n23:02 How I Realized Sugar Was Destroying My Life\n\n25:42 Sugar Was Hurting My Brain\n\n26:52 Breaking Free: The How of Cutting Sugar\n\n27:30 #1 Break The Habit - Substitution With A Twist\n\n29:00 Why Substitution Typically Fails\n\n35:31 #2 - Eat More Food - Real Protein, Fats & Fiber\n\n35:50 Are Sugar Cravings A Signal For Protein\n\n40:15 Navigating Sugar in Daily Life\n\n44:05 Teaching Kids About Sugar and Self-Control\n\nAI OVERVIEW\n\nIn this episode, Norbie Schickel discusses the pervasive presence of sugar in the American diet, its health implications, and its connection to mental health. He shares personal experiences with sugar addiction and offers strategies for breaking the habit. The conversation also touches on the importance of educating future generations about sugar consumption and making healthier choices.\n\n#sugarfree #metabolichealth #mentalhealth\n\n## Page Links\n\n- https://www.be-unconditional.com/\n- https://www.be-unconditional.com/follow/\n- https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/id1836510781?mt=2&amp;ls=1\n- https://open.spotify.com/show/0tvViBZhvXS9x7vKgs4JvM\n- https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=MPSPPLffPW9KS5qFcixzGA5_tjYKzI4zk9Qiy2\n- https://www.be-unconditional.com/episodes/\n- https://www.be-unconditional.com/about/\n- https://www.be-unconditional.com/contact/\n- https://www.be-unconditional.com/how-ultra-processed-foods-took-over-the-world/\n- https://www.be-unconditional.com/what-everyone-gets-wrong-about-dr-weston-a-price-including-his-fans-ep-28/\n- https://www.be-unconditional.com/science-says-working-out-wont-help-you-lose-weight-the-energy-paradox-ep-27/\n- https://www.be-unconditional.com/ultra-processed-foods-the-study-that-changed-everything-and-what-it-missed-ep-26/\n- https://www.be-unconditional.com/the-not-so-obvious-case-for-staying-natty-ep-25/\n- https://www.be-unconditional.com/carbs-vs-fat-metabolic-health-weight-loss-gold-standard-science-ep-24/\n- https://www.be-unconditional.com/the-four-horseman-of-the-aging-apocalypse-training-longevity-attia-ep-23/\n- https://www.be-unconditional.com/jacked-without-the-gym-build-muscle-burn-fat-with-bands-bells-bodyweight-ep-22/\n- https://www.podpage.com/?utm_source=podpage_podcast_website&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=podpage_footer&utm_content=unconditional\n","title":"Sugar Was Turning Me Into A Monster. Here's How I Broke Free | E…","httpStatus":200},"sequence_number":726}

data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","output_index":20,"item":{"id":"st_tmp_p7wlnfxs75l","type":"openrouter:web_fetch","status":"completed","url":"https://podcast.nettagorman.com/episode-175/","content":"\"Now I feel free from the hold sugar had on me\": Danielle (Episode 175) - Life After Sugar Podcast\n\n# Listen to episode 175:\n\n# \"Now I feel free from the hold sugar had on me\": Danielle\n\nMay 19, 2024\n\nDanielle's journey with sugar started in childhood. She remembers that sugar was a massive part of her upbringing.\n\nWith her family, she always had ice cream after dinner. Sugar was always a treat.They even had a trunk in their house that had little goodie bags with sweet treats for whenever she and her brother were good.\n\nSo there was a lot of rewarding with sugar.As a child, Danielle was an extremely picky eater. She ate lots of carbs, like white pasta and rice cakes... which, she says, no doubt really put her on a blood sugar roller coaster at a very young age.\n\nDanielle says that sugar was the coping and addictive mechanisms that had been handed down through her family line. Her mom, she explains, was someone who never felt emotions, and she used food to numb and escape. So Danielle got that pattern from her.\n\nBut then in her late twenties, Danielle started looking more deeply into her early childhood traumas and what contributed to the addictive patterning in her brain.And that was the start of an awakening for her.\n\nListen to Danielle describe her slow 3-year process to finally feel free from the hold sugar had on her.\n\nGet rid of cravings so that you can slim down and finally feel in control around food!\n\nTake the first step to get rid of cravings:\n\nDo the Cravings Quiz!\n\nGet personalized guidance from me, plus support and accountability in a small group... in the 90-day Freedom from Cravings Formulaprogram.\n\nSEE ALSO:\n\nClick here to listen\n\nClick here to listen\n\nClick here to listen\n\nClick here to listen\n\nClick here to listen\n\nClick here to listen\n\nUse the Search bar below to find an episode number, topic or guest:\n\nSearch\n\nListen on any of these podcast platforms and subscribe:\n\nListen on Apple Podcasts\n\nListen on Google Podcasts\n\nAlso check out the Life After Sugar Facebook page, and subscribe to my Instagram account and to the Life After Sugar YouTube channel.\n\nTo rate and review this podcast:\n\n1. scroll down in your podcast player on your phone and click on the stars.\n2. To leave a review, scroll down a little more and click on \"Write a Review\".\n3. Once you’ve finished, select “Send” or “Save” in the top-right corner.\n4. If you’ve never left a podcast review before, enter a nickname. Your nickname will be displayed on your review.\n5. After selecting a nickname, tap OK. Your review may not be immediately visible, but it should be posted soon. Thank you! - Netta\n\nGET RID OF YOUR CRAVINGS\n\n## and find peace with food\n\n##### Grab these 5 tips now to help get rid of your cravings!\n\nYES! I WANT TO GET RID OF CRAVINGS!\n\n#### ALL EPISODES >>\n\n## Page Links\n\n- https://podcast.nettagorman.com/\n- https://sugarcravingsfree.com/book/\n- https://danielledaem.com/\n- https://sugarcravingsfree.com/cravings-quiz\n- https://sugarcravingsfree.com/\n- https://podcast.nettagorman.com/episode-067/\n- https://podcast.nettagorman.com/episode-247/\n- https://podcast.nettagorman.com/episode-045/\n- https://podcast.nettagorman.com/episode-090/\n- https://podcast.nettagorman.com/episode-144/\n- https://podcast.nettagorman.com/episode-084/\n- https://podcasts.apple.com/podcast/id1546092478\n- https://open.spotify.com/show/4J0JySp6hdi9g2rhaKSR03\n- https://podcasts.google.com/feed/aHR0cHM6Ly9mZWVkcy5idXp6c3Byb3V0LmNvbS8xNDk5NzUyLnJzcw==\n- https://www.iheart.com/podcast/269-life-after-sugar-74970422/\n- https://www.facebook.com/mylifeaftersugar\n- https://www.instagram.com/mylifeaftersugar/\n- https://www.youtube.com/c/LifeAfterSugar/videos\n- https://sugarcravingsfree.com/5-tips\n- https://sugarcravingsfree.com/success-stories/\n- https://sugarcravingsfree.com/contact/\n- https://sugarcravingsfree.com/privacy-policy/\n","title":"\"Now I feel free from the hold sugar had on me\": Danielle (Episode 175) - Life After Sugar Podcast","httpStatus":200},"sequence_number":727}

data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","output_index":21,"item":{"id":"st_tmp_lt9k0i6jwpl","type":"openrouter:web_fetch","status":"completed","url":"https://thisnakedmind.com/ep-269-breaking-up-with-sugar-with-molly-carmel/","content":"EP 269: Breaking Up with Sugar with Molly Carmel - This Naked Mind\n\n# EP 269: Breaking Up with Sugar with Molly Carmel\n\nOn today’s episode, Annie Grace talks with fellow brain science lover Molly Carmel, an eating disorders and addictions therapist and author of Breaking Up with Sugar. Molly shares her story – from the beginning of her relationship with sugar in response to a childhood trauma to their breakup over 10 years ago – including how Molly ate her way through bariatric surgery and ultimately got rid of dieting, changed her relationship with food, and lost 175 pounds.\n\nHave you tried The Alcohol Experiment? Okay, if not, drop everything and go to thisnakedmind.com/experiment. This free 30-day challenge is designed to interrupt your patterns and put you back in touch with the best version of you. You remember, it was that version of you that’s living your most joyful life, the version that doesn’t need alcohol to relax or to have a good time, and is having more fun than ever. Again, this is a totally free challenge that will change everything for you. So learn more and join me 100% free at thisnakedmind.com/experiment.\n\nAnd as always, rate, review, and subscribe to this podcast, as it truly helps the message reach somebody who might need to hear it today.\n\n## Share Your Story\n\nDid This Naked Mind, The PATH, or The Alcohol Experiment help you find freedom from drinking? Share your story and you could be featured on an episode of This Naked Mind Podcast to inspire others. Find out how here!\n\nDownload Transcript\n\n## Related Episodes\n\n### Annie Grace on the Feel Lit Alcohol Free Podcast | E779\n\nListen Now\n\n### EP 689: Interview with Dr. Melissa Kalt\n\nListen Now\n\n### EP 667: Medicinal and Functional Mushrooms with Hamilton\n\nListen Now\n\n### Annie Grace on the Feel Lit Alcohol Free Podcast | E779\n\nListen Now\n\n### EP 689: Interview with Dr. Melissa Kalt\n\nListen Now\n\n### EP 667: Medicinal and Functional Mushrooms with Hamilton\n\nListen Now\n\n# Curious about all the amazing benefits a break from alcohol can bring?\n\nJoin us for a FREE Alcohol Experiment\n\n#### About\n\n#### Resources\n\n#### Books\n\n#### Press\n\nPrivacy Policy| Terms of Service| Contact Us| Login\n\n## Page Links\n\n- https://go.tnmprograms.com/start-here-quiz\n- https://shop.thisnakedmind.com/?_gl=1*hlc4k6*_ga*MTYzNTIwMzMxOS4xNzQ3ODA3NTk1*_ga_EQS6MLGRQL*czE3NDgzMTQ2NzckbzE3JGcxJHQxNzQ4MzE2MTEzJGo2MCRsMCRoMCRkVjUwNjRVcmYtMHpCSHdGc1V4eVhvTzM4SGtOY1Zhd25VQQ..\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/programs-training/\n- https://www.thisnakedmind.com/experiment\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/this-naked-mind/\n- http://nakedmindpath.com/\n- http://www.alcoholexperiment.com/\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/my-story/\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/annie-grace-on-the-feel-lit-alcohol-free-podcast-e779/\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/ep-689-interview-with-dr-melissa-kalt/\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/ep-667-medicinal-and-functional-mushrooms-with-hamilton/\n- http://www.thealcoholexperiment.com/\n- https://shop.thisnakedmind.com/\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/contact-us\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/jobs/\n- http://www.applytnmi.com/\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/coaching/\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/reviews/\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/strategy-process/\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/our-movement/\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/annie-grace/\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/podcasts/\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/blog/\n- https://thisnakedmind.com/weekly-newsletter/\n- https://learn.thisnakedmind.com/6-booze-breaking-tips-request?_gl=1*ds4ad3*_ga*MTYzNTIwMzMxOS4xNzQ3ODA3NTk1*_ga_EQS6MLGRQL*czE3NDgzMTQ2NzckbzE3JGcxJHQxNzQ4MzE2MTEzJGo2MCRsMCRoMCRkVjUwNjRVcmYtMHpCSHdGc1V4eVhvTzM4SGtOY1Zhd25VQQ..\n- https://download.canimodera