data: {"type":"response.output_text.annotation.added","output_index":43,"item_id":"msg_tmp_5gg2b6kmfyx","content_index":0,"annotation_index":3,"annotation":{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0Pz7Sq4_HOA","title":"I Quit Sugar for 8 Months. Here's How.","start_index":0,"end_index":0},"sequence_number":2869}

data: {"type":"response.output_text.annotation.added","output_index":43,"item_id":"msg_tmp_5gg2b6kmfyx","content_index":0,"annotation_index":4,"annotation":{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SQkCUyNeiQw","title":"","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"## Transcript\n\n[...]\n\nI quit sugar for 90 days and I genuinely didn't expect this I wasn't expecting it to transform so many areas in my life I don't feel as tired during the day I don't need to take a nap after lunch anymore I lost a lot of belly fat I gained strength at the gym but mostly I'm just feeling more alert during the day but there's a reason why I quit sugar in the first place right so let's rewind to earlier this year I hit a plateau at the gym I just couldn't put on any more muscle I couldn't lose any more fat even though I was strength training regularly I was boxing I was living relatively healthily so whenever I get stuck with pretty much anything really I go out and I find someone that's really good in that specific area and ask them for advice so I did my research I found the most qualified personal trainer I could find in the city he's ridiculously qualified trained celebrities actors that kind of thing and in the first training session we spent about two to three hours talking about my lifestyle and diet anyway long story short he mentioned that I consume way too much sugar I ate so much fruit I drank fruit juices every day I ate yogurts every day I thought that I was eating healthily and I mean fruit is good for you but maybe eating 9 10 11 fruit a day well that is a lot of sugar straight away he put me on a sugar-free diet with no carbohydrates and I had to drink three liters of water a day which was ironically the hardest part of the whole kind of diet I had never done anything like that before so I was super super strict and for the first 30 days when I mean my diet with sugar and carb-free it really was within literally about three or four days I started to notice the differences mainly I had more energy throughout the day and I felt less bloated after meals that was quite a big one however pretty quickly things started it going downhill I remember with day six and seven my energy levels absolutely crashed I mean I was so exhausted literally I couldn't even move and that's no exaggeration I don't really know what that was whether it was my body kind of reacting badly I don't know but looking back that was the only negative side effect I experienced and that only lasted for like one or two days I remember I was so tired that I missed the week of uploading videos on this YouTube channel and that almost never happens\n\n[...]\n\nhave since kind of introduced it back into my diet by about 20 right because if I'm going to keep this up long term and I mean for years then it needs to be easy right and completely cutting sugar out 100 is not easy at all for me anyways but cutting Sugar by 80 okay okay that's a lot easier and that's all I really care about is consistency as long as I keep 80 of the benefits that I've been experiencing then it's all good it's the same with cutting carbohydrates out of my diet too I've since added about 20 of carbs back into my diet completely for the sake of consistency and Longevity I see this as a lifestyle not a short-term diet and when I add sugar and carbs back into my diet by 20 that's actually super easy to maintain long term exactly how it should be also I do have to mention that I am not recommending you to completely quit sugar or carbs I'm not a dietitian I'm not a nutritionist I'm just kind of reporting back the results that I've been seeing for myself everyone's body will obviously react differently although saying that I think I can safely say that if you do want to make some immediate changes with your diet cutting out or at least significantly decreasing sugar so not cutting out but decreasing it from your diet and drinking two to three liters of water a day and maybe even slightly cutting carbs a little bit could be a good start quitting sugar and just cleaning up my kind of diet in general is probably the I would say the second best decision I've made in terms of improving My overall health the best decision I've made though is learning how to fix my sleeping pattern meaning learning how to wake up early and not feel tired in fact I recently uploaded a video titled I woke up at 4 45 AM for 906 days going through the steps that I took you can click on the card on the screen to watch that alternatively I made another video called train yourself to learn like Einstein that video is popping off right now again you can click on the card on the screen to watch that\n\n[...]\n\n## Chapters\n\n- 00:00 Benefits of quitting sugar\n- 00:22 Why I quit sugar\n- 01:42 What I noticed after 3-4 days of quitting sugar\n- 01:57 What I noticed after 6-7 days of quitting sugar\n- 04:22 What I noticed after 14 days of quitting sugar\n- 05:24 The biggest thing I've learned from quitting sugar for 90 days\n- 06:33 Important disclaimer\n\n[...]\n\ncan count on one hand how often I forget to miss a weekly video upload in six years of running this Channel and that's pretty impressive consistency because being a content creator and uploading every single week for years is not easy but this video sponsor epidemic sounds makes being a content creator that bit easier so epidemic sounds is where I get my music from for this channel the background music that you're listening to right now is from there it's a great tool for video creators to to soundtrack their videos without receiving copyright strikes or worrying about takedowns it saves my video editors so much time because they don't have to search for ages to find decent royalty-free music\n\n[...]\n\nfact I had this discussion with them a couple of months ago now actually they tried a lot of different royalty-free music platforms but epidemic sounds is the only subscription that they keep asking me to renew their subscription for it is from our experience anyway the platform with the widest range of Music where all tracks are professionally produced by a really wide range of artists so it saves them a lot of time because they can find music very easily and one of my favorite features is that if you find a song that you like you can click the find similar icon and it will throw up a list of songs that are similar again it just makes finding music for my videos that much easier so epidemic sounds have a personal plan which\n\n[...]\n\nsecond thing I noticed the belly fat around my abs pretty much went in just 30 40 days which I was really surprised about and my strength at the gym was going up and soap so I was losing weight and getting stronger at the gym it's also worth noticing that I didn't notice much when drinking three liters of water a day I haven't noticed any positive or negative effects from this other than having to go to the toilet more often but I know it's healthy to stay hydrated and I'm living in quite a hot climate so that's why I maintain that even though I'm not seeing any direct benefits so what's the biggest thing that I've learned from quitting sugar for 90 days I've learned that honestly I love sugar way too much I really do have a sweet tooth and so since cutting sugar completely 490 days\n\n[...]\n\nideal for Content creators and a commercial plan for Freelancers and businesses\n\n[...]\n\nI can remember the last time that my energy levels have been this stable\n\n[...]\n\nas a direct result I'm more focused at work and my productivity has increased significantly\n\n[...]\n\n've tried a lot of royalty-free music platforms epidemic Sounds by far the best in my opinion so back to my food Journey over the last year or so about two weeks into cutting sugar this is where the magic kind of happened in the second week that's when I really started to feel the most improvements in my everyday life so I started to feel much more energized I stopped to experience those kind of massive drops in energy in the afternoon\n\n[...]\n\n# I Quit Sugar for 90 Days (it’s changing my life)\n\n[...]\n\n30-day free trial if you use my link in the description\n\n[...]\n\nthat's actually the plan that my team and I use so if you want to check epidemic sounds out you can get\n\n[...]\n\nI really recommend you do try them out\n\n[...]\n\nMi"},"sequence_number":2870}

data: {"type":"response.output_text.annotation.added","output_index":43,"item_id":"msg_tmp_5gg2b6kmfyx","content_index":0,"annotation_index":5,"annotation":{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://fight.fudgie.org/search/show/oz/episode/20250115_Wed_9mX8Ang_bZk","title":"Dr. Oz Podcast - Your Guide to Quitting Sugar with Dr. Joel Fuhrman | Dr. Oz | S7 | Ep 131 | Full Episode - Transcript","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"##### Your Guide to Quitting Sugar with Dr. Joel Fuhrman | Dr. Oz | S7 | Ep 131 | Full Episode\n\n[...]\n\nDr. Joel Fuhrman details quitting sugar's life-saving benefits, citing a study where blood pressure dropped 26 points and heart disease risk fell threefold by eliminating toxic foods. He introduces \"The Sweet Six\" for dessert cravings and advocates vegetable-first meals, noting Darcy lost 90 pounds via high-fiber salads. The episode also previews Dr. Delaney Rustin's \"Screen Agers,\" linking screens to immature prefrontal cortices, while Simon Sinek compares smartphone addiction to open liquor cabinets. Finally, Fuhrman suggests replacing salt with herbs like oregano and cinnamon to reduce inflammation. [Automatically generated summary]\n\n[...]\n\n131 | Full Episode - Transcript\n\n[...]\n\nDr. Oz Podcast - Your Guide to Quitting Sugar with Dr. Joel Fuhrman | Dr. Oz | S7 | Ep\n\n[...]\n\nTranscriber: large-v3-turbo\n\n[...]\n\nOz Podcast\n\n[...]\n\n► 00:02:13 | You know, I just published a study in the American Journal of Lifestyle Medicine on 443 people with high blood pressure. Sign in to favourite this quote |\n\n[...]\n\n► 00:03:50 | In fact, cutting sugars from your diet will reduce your risk of dying from heart-related issues by about three times. Sign in to favourite this quote |\n\n[...]\n\nJan. 15, 2025 - Dr\n\n[...]\n\n| ► 00:02:21 | They dropped their blood pressure 26 points. Sign in to favourite this quote |\n\n[...]\n\n,\n\n[...]\n\n# the sweet six\n\n[...]\n\nbig\n\n[...]\n\nit\n\n[...]\n\n| ► 00:03:56 | It plummets threefold. Sign in to favourite this quote |\n\n[...]\n\nHe says that removing toxic foods like\n\n[...]\n\n► 00:06:12 | In fact, Joel, he calls this thing, it's very interesting, the Sweet Six. Sign in to favourite this quote |\n\n[...]\n\n| ► 00:02:19 | They normalized their LDL cholesterol. Sign in to favourite this quote |\n\n[...]\n\nBut"},"sequence_number":2871}

data: {"type":"response.output_text.annotation.added","output_index":43,"item_id":"msg_tmp_5gg2b6kmfyx","content_index":0,"annotation_index":6,"annotation":{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://thefastingmethodpodcast.libsyn.com/quitting-sugar-without-the-all-or-nothing-trap","title":"The Fasting Method Podcast: Quitting Sugar Without the All-or-Nothing Trap","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"In this episode, Coaches Terri and Heather explore what actually happens when people try to quit sugar — especially when perfectionism and cultural pressure get in the way. They discuss the common fear of “missing out,” why short-term challenges can be powerful experiments, and how reducing sugar can quiet food noise, reduce cravings, and improve fasting success.\n\n[...]\n\n👉 What you’ll learn: • Why perfectionism sabotages most sugar resets • How catastrophizing keeps people stuck • Why short-term challenges are easier to commit to than lifelong rules • What happens to cravings and food noise when insulin drops • How cultural and family traditions influence food choices • The difference between moderation and abstinence • Why “dose makes the poison” • How to evaluate whether sugar truly adds value to your life\n\n[...]\n\nRather than framing sugar as a lifelong ban, this conversation focuses on practical experience: What happens when you step away for 30 days? What do you learn? And how do you avoid the all-or-nothing trap that derails so many attempts at change?\n\n[...]\n\nWhat really happens when you try to quit sugar — and why perfection isn’t required to experience freedom.\n\n[...]\n\n📝 Transcript The transcript for this episode is available on our website: https://www.thefastingmethod.com/podcasts/\n\n[...]\n\n⏱️ Timestamps 00:00 — Sugar and the “but I like it” belief 02:11 — The idea of a “Free February” reset 04:08 — What the no sugar, no grains challenge revealed 06:27 — Why perfectionism derails progress 09:03 — Culture, holidays, and food identity 12:10 — Why short-term experiments work 13:48 — The early discomfort phase 16:15 — Sugar is everywhere: environmental priming 19:22 — Would your event really be better with sugar? 22:28 — Vacation, Disney, and defined indulgence rules 24:29 — Touching the hot stove: learning from experience 25:31 — Final reflections and encouragement\n\n[...]\n\n## Quitting Sugar Without the All-or-Nothing Trap\n\n[...]\n\nThe Fasting Method Podcast: Quitting Sugar Without the All-or-Nothing Trap\n\n[...]\n\n### Quitting Sugar Without the All-or-Nothing Trap\n\n[...]\n\nEpisode #246 🎙️ You don’t have to be perfect to change your relationship with sugar.\n\n[...]\n\nhttps://thefastingmethodpodcast.libsyn.com/quitting-sugar-without-the-all-or-nothing-trap\n\n[...]\n\n# The Fasting Method Podcast\n\n[...]\n\n/\n\n[...]\n\ning"},"sequence_number":2872}

