data: {"type":"response.output_text.annotation.added","output_index":43,"item_id":"msg_tmp_5gg2b6kmfyx","content_index":0,"annotation_index":29,"annotation":{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://www.buzzsprout.com/2359869/episodes/19327321-breaking-free-from-sugar-addiction-with-mike-collins","title":"Breaking Free From Sugar Addiction with Mike Collins","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"Mike shares his personal journey, the science behind sugar cravings, why traditional diet advice often fails, and how a structured sugar detox can help people reclaim their health, mental clarity, and emotional resilience.\n\n[...]\n\nIn this eye-opening conversation, Jeanne Collins sits down with Mike Collins, founder of SugarAddiction.com and known online as the Sugar Free Man, to explore the powerful connection between sugar, emotional health, addiction, and long-term wellness.\n\n[...]\n\nWhether you're curious about reducing sugar, overcoming cravings, or creating lasting lifestyle change, this episode offers practical insights and a fresh perspective on what true wellness really means.\n\n[...]\n\n]Mike Collins believes sugar addiction is very real and not to be taken lightly. As a person in long-term recovery from substance use disorder for over forty years, he took a keen interest in what sugar was doing to him and his friends in early recovery. After much research and experimentation, he quit sugar with the help of amazing mentors. He then raised two children sugar-free from the womb to six years old, and as they grew, he rewrote the rules for sugar and kids in childhood. He takes his stewardship of SugarAddiction.com, SugarDetox.com, and QuitSugarSummit.com very seriously and aims to provide information and community for anyone wanting to curb or quit sugar.Hundreds of thousands have read his book The Last Resort Sugar Detox, and tens of thousands have completed his online 30-Day Sugar Freedom Challenge.\n\n[...]\n\nThe\n\n[...]\n\n90-Day Sugar Detox Process\n\n[...]\n\n##\n\n[...]\n\nand we are going\n\n[...]\n\nSugar is everywhere—but what if it’s influencing far more than your waistline?\n\n[...]\n\nact\n\n[...]\n\nfrom their lives. And I personally love sugar. I know it's not great for me. I don't use\n\n[...]\n\nThen\n\n[...]\n\njob\n\n[...]\n\nshe\n\n[...]\n\n. Welcome to the show, everybody. I'm your host, Gene Collins, and today we're\n\n[...]\n\n0\n\n[...]\n\n.\n\n[...]\n\n0:04\n\n[...]\n\nHe's got a book, he\n\n[...]\n\na lot, but I love even natural sugar. I really love it. So I am fascinated to learn all about how Mike became the expert in helping people detox\n\n[...]\n\ncoming up, and I cannot tell you how many people were so interested in this subject. So Mike is an expert at helping people detox and\n\n[...]\n\nWelcome to Building the Best You, a destination for you to reimagine what is possible in your life and then create\n\n[...]\n\nreality.\n\n[...]\n\nthe\n\n[...]\n\nWe're talking to Mike Collins"},"sequence_number":2895}

data: {"type":"response.output_text.annotation.added","output_index":43,"item_id":"msg_tmp_5gg2b6kmfyx","content_index":0,"annotation_index":30,"annotation":{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://annalaurabrown.com/how-to-quit-sugar-addition-now/","title":"How to Quit Sugar Addiction for Better Health - Holistic Autoimmune Healing","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"Laura"},"sequence_number":2896}

data: {"type":"response.output_text.annotation.added","output_index":43,"item_id":"msg_tmp_5gg2b6kmfyx","content_index":0,"annotation_index":31,"annotation":{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://www.buzzsprout.com/1899455/episodes/17275283-bitten-jonsson-the-reality-of-sugar-addiction-recovery","title":"Bitten Jonsson: The Reality of Sugar Addiction Recovery","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"In this candid conversation, Bitten shares her own relapse story during menopause, reveals why traditional recovery methods often fail, and explains why she believes ketogenic eating is crucial for lasting freedom. She doesn't sugarcoat the reality: recovery rates are low, relapse is common, and our toxic food environment makes healing harder than ever\n\n[...]\n\nAs Sweden's leading sugar addiction expert and registered nurse, Bitten discovered her food addiction while already in recovery from alcoholism. What started as a personal struggle became her life's work—training coaches and medical professionals to treat what she calls \"the strongest psychoactive substance on earth.\"\n\n[...]\n\nand shares the daily practices that have kept her free for decades\n\n[...]\n\nBut there's hope. After decades of working with thousands of clients, Bitten has developed methods that work. She explains why treating addiction must come first, before trauma work or therapy\n\n[...]\n\nBitten Johnson has been sober from alcohol for 39 years, but quitting sugar? That was the real battle.\n\n[...]\n\nWhether you're struggling with food cravings yourself or trying to understand why willpower isn't enough, this interview offers rare insights from someone who's walked the path and dedicated her life to lighting the way for others."},"sequence_number":2897}

