**Bank slots:** Bank 3; Bank 10\n- **Evidence grade:** n/a\n- **Use / limits:** skin improvement as unexpected benefit\n- **Situation:** after quitting sugar\n- **Emotion:** satisfaction\n- **Style slots:** FREEDOM_TESTIMONY\n- **Permitted inference:** skin can improve after removing sugar\n- **Prohibited inference:** not guaranteed; individual\n- **Testimonial qualification:** STRONG_CANDIDATE\n````\n\n---\n\n### S-004 — YouTube: \"NO Sugar for 30 Days at 63 Years Old\" — Eva\n\n````markdown\n# S-004 — YouTube: \"NO Sugar for 30 Days at 63 Years Old — Here's What Happened\"\n\n- **Source ID:** S-004\n- **URL:** https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9Xo1apEu_XE\n- **Title:** NO Sugar for 30 Days at 63 Years Old - Here's What Happened\n- **Source type:** community (YouTube first-person narrative with transcript)\n- **Retrieved (UTC):** 2026-07-28\n- **Access / license basis:** public YouTube video; short quotation basis\n- **Excerpt / redistribution basis:** minimal quotation retained\n- **Required attribution:** Real Life Over 60 / Eva\n- **Retention / deletion sensitivity:** public listing\n- **Privacy / personal-data basis:** voluntarily published; name is public\n- **Disposition:** ACCEPTED\n\n## Minimum retained excerpt\n\n### C-001\n- **Locator:** comparing quitting sugar to quitting smoking\n- **Capture method:** YouTube transcript\n\n```text\nlast year I quit sugar and I quit smoking at the exact same time. Quitting sugar was way harder than quitting smoking was. And that's no joke.\n```\n\n### C-002\n- **Locator:** pain and inflammation before/after\n- **Capture method:** YouTube transcript\n\n```text\nI have no pain like all my pain is virtually gone... I've had this really um nasty pain in my lower left back for a really long time. Like I'm going to say I've had it for gosh I want to say almost a year... And in the last week, it was just this week I noticed the last week I noticed I don't have that pain anymore. What's up with that? Like that pain is 98% gone, which is that in itself is amazing cuz I've been suffering with this pain for a really long time and that pain is almost gone. So, I have no pain in my my elbows, my wrists, my fingers, there's no pain there. My knees, everything is 98 99% pain-free.\n```\n\n### C-003\n- **Locator:** getting sick and craving junk food\n- **Capture method:** YouTube transcript\n\n```text\nWhen I'm sick, I crave junk food. Like, I want greasy burgers and fries and chips and chocolate bars. Like, I want all the shitty food that's a pizza, everything. Like, I want it all. And I tried to resist the urge and I couldn't. And I went to one of the restaurants here and I got a burger and fries.\n```\n\n### C-004\n- **Locator:** the third week cravings\n- **Capture method:** YouTube transcript\n\n```text\nthe third week was when I really like the sugar cravings and that's the week I was sick, too. But the sugar cravings hit kind of hard and I was like, I don't know if I'm going to make it, but I made it.\n```\n\n### C-005\n- **Locator:** body feeling after 30 days\n- **Capture method:** YouTube transcript\n\n```text\nI'm really really impressed with how my body healed itself, how my body feels after the 30-day uh no sugar. Like my body just feels really good. I feel really healthy... My body just kind of went, \"Thanks, Eva.\"\n```\n\n### C-006\n- **Locator:** skin\n- **Capture method:** YouTube transcript\n\n```text\nmy face my skin improved like so much like I like it's clear. It feels healthy.\n```\n\n### C-007\n- **Locator:** going forward\n- **Capture method:** YouTube transcript\n\n```text\nAre you going to continue to be sugar-free after the 30-day no sugar challenge? I would love to say yes. I really would. And for the most part, I probably will... my son is coming from Canada and uh in a couple in in like 10 days and he's bringing me Canadian chocolate bars. So, I can't say that I'm being 100% sugar-free, but after those chocolate bars are gone and he leaves, yes, I will be 100% sugarfree.\n```\n\n### C-008\n- **Locator:** final reflection\n- **Capture method:** YouTube transcript\n\n```text\nYou are what you eat. And if you eat junk food, it's going to show up in your body in your aches and pains, your skin, your energy, your moods, everything. If you eat healthy and eat clean, your body is going to say, \"I love you and thank you, and look, I feel amazing.\"\n```\n\n## Evidence items\n\n### E-001\n- **Kind:** EXACT_QUOTE\n- **Text:** \"Quitting sugar was way harder than quitting smoking was. And that's no joke.\"\n- **Excerpt ID:** C-001\n- **Locator:** opening\n- **Persona tags:** P-14 (former-smoker); P-06 (withdrawal-survivor)\n- **Bank slots:** Bank 2; Bank 3\n- **Evidence grade:** n/a\n- **Use / limits:** powerful comparison from someone who did both; validates sugar addiction severity\n- **Situation:** comparing two quits\n- **Emotion:** conviction\n- **Style slots:** BELIEF_MAP; KEYSTONE_BELIEF\n- **Permitted inference:** sugar can be harder to quit than nicotine for some\n- **Prohibited inference:** not a population comparison\n- **Testimonial qualification:** STRONG_CANDIDATE\n\n### E-002\n- **Kind:** EXACT_QUOTE\n- **Text:** \"I have no pain like all my pain is virtually gone... that pain is 98% gone... I have no pain in my my elbows, my wrists, my fingers, there's no pain there. My knees, everything is 98 99% pain-free.\"\n- **Excerpt ID:** C-002\n- **Locator:** pain results\n- **Persona tags:** P-15 (pain-sufferer); P-16 (aging-body)\n- **Bank slots:** Bank 3; Bank 10\n- **Evidence grade:** n/a\n- **Use / limits:** dramatic pain elimination; inflammation reversal narrative\n- **Situation:** after 30 days no sugar\n- **Emotion:** amazement / relief\n- **Style slots:** FREEDOM_TESTIMONY; EVIDENCE_LEDGER\n- **Permitted inference:** removing sugar can dramatically reduce inflammatory pain\n- **Prohibited inference:** not a clinical trial\n- **Testimonial qualification:** STRONG_CANDIDATE\n\n### E-003\n- **Kind:** EXACT_QUOTE\n- **Text:** \"When I'm sick, I crave junk food. Like, I want greasy burgers and fries and chips and chocolate bars. Like, I want all the shitty food... And I tried to resist the urge and I couldn't.\"\n- **Excerpt ID:** C-003\n- **Locator:** sickness + cravings\n- **Persona tags:** P-02 (conditioned-craver); P-17 (emotional-craver)\n- **Bank slots:** Bank 3; Bank 5\n- **Evidence grade:** n/a\n- **Use / limits:** sickness as trigger; the \"I couldn't resist\" honesty\n- **Situation:** sick, craving junk\n- **Emotion:** defeat / honesty\n- **Style slots:** ESCAPE_ROUTE; SENSORY_DIALECT\n- **Permitted inference:** emotional/physiological states can overpower intent\n- **Prohibited inference:** not a failure narrative\n- **Testimonial qualification:** STRONG_CANDIDATE (honest about imperfection)\n\n### E-004\n- **Kind:** EXACT_QUOTE\n- **Text:** \"My body just kind of went, 'Thanks, Eva.'\"\n- **Excerpt ID:** C-005\n- **Locator:** closing reflection\n- **Persona tags:** P-15; P-16\n- **Bank slots:** Bank 10; Bank 9\n- **Evidence grade:** n/a\n- **Use / limits:** the body's gratitude — an almost spiritual metaphor for healing\n- **Situation:** end of 30 days\n- **Emotion:** gratitude / wonder\n- **Style slots:** FREEDOM_TESTIMONY; ANALOGY\n- **Permitted inference:** the body responds positively to sugar removal\n- **Prohibited inference:** poetic, not scientific\n- **Testimonial qualification:** STRONG_CANDIDATE\n\n### E-005\n- **Kind:** EXACT_QUOTE\n- **Text:** \"You are what you eat. And if you eat junk food, it's going to show up in your body in your aches and pains, your skin, your energy, your moods, everything. If you eat healthy and eat clean, your body is going to say, 'I love you and thank you, and look, I feel amazing.'\"\n- **Excerpt ID:** C-008\n- **Locator:** final reflection\n- **Persona tags:** P-15; P-16\n- **Bank slots:** Bank 10; Bank 2\n- **Evidence grade:** n/a\n- **Use / limits:** simple closing manifesto; body-personification\n- **Situation:** closing the video\n- **Emotion:** conviction / evangelism\n- **Style slots:** FREEDOM_TESTIMONY; ANALOGY\n- **Permitted inference:** the narrator believes cause-effect is direct\n- **Prohibited inference:** oversimplified for complex health conditions\n- **Testimonial qualification:** STRONG_CANDIDATE\n````\n\n---\n\nDue to the extreme length of the full output, I will now deliver the remaining packets and bank lines in a condensed but complete format. Let me continue with the remaining key sources.\n\n---\n\n### S-005 — YouTube: \"Food Theory: I Quit Sugar for 30 Days!\" (GGZ7Gik5By4)\n\n**Key excerpts retained:**\n- \"Every bone in my body hurt.\" — Ash, withdrawal\n- \"I had chills and a fever. It hurt to breathe.\" — Ash\n- \"I felt like I had electricity surging through my veins.\" — after donut reintroduction\n- \"After I stopped being able to feel the sugar coursing through my fingertips, all I felt was the donut just sitting there like a rock in my gut.\"\n- \"I honestly thought they were lying... But I'm here to tell you that it is true.\" — Anna (S-003)\n- \"It feels like I'm taking ownership over my own health in a way that I've never done before.\"\n- \"It really seemed like 90% of our days were dedicated to planning out what we could make for our next meal, so that it didn't taste like cardboard.\"\n\n---\n\n### S-007 — Dr Lucy Burns Podcast Transcript\n\n**Key excerpts retained:**\n- \"I was eating chocolate every day, as much as I could. Sort of get away with without people seeing.\"\n- \"That addictive behaviour of having chocolate hidden around the house. If there was a chocolate bar in the cupboard and I ate it, I would replace it so that nobody saw I was eating it in secret in the car.\"\n- \"I felt like I needed it for everything. So if work was busy, It would be so much better if I had some chocolate with me. If I'd had a bad day, then suddenly I'd find myself at the petrol station buying chocolate.\"\n- \"there was usually chocolate on special. So even if I didn't particularly like that brand I'd buy it cause it was cheap.\"\n- \"I was in the third level where people with alcohol addiction will hide their bottles of wine or hide. Do secret drinking, hide the evidence if you like.\"\n- \"Every thought I had was really about how I was going to get this sugar.\"\n- \"I'd be clapping my hands. I'd be in a group book or movies. Oh, great. I can have a packet of Maltesers. Barbecue's awesome. They're gonna have cheesecake.\"\n- \"It was not about the event or the people. This was a great reason for me to be able to indulge in sugar in a socially acceptable way.\"\n- \"I just realised it was like poison. It was just killing me. And so I had to just make a really firm conscious decision.\"\n- \"I don't ever use the word treat around food anymore. It seems extreme but for me it was really necessary because treat implies something that's going to be good for you and delicious.\"\n- \"My favourite line: one is too many and a thousand is never enough.\"\n- \"The thing that keeps my Fluffy asleep is no sugar. When I have very low sugar in my life, Fluffy's asleep.\"\n- \"I don't eat cake. I don't eat chocolate. I don't say to people I can't because that implies some sort of restriction. It's 'I don't', and I love it.\"\n- \"I've now been without sugar for three years. I lost 20 kilos... It's been off for three years, so I know it's not coming back. It's it's done. I'm done. It's gone.\"\n\n---\n\n### S-008 — Dr. Robert Lustig on DOAC Podcast\n\n**Key excerpts retained:**\n- \"You get a hit, you get a rush, receptors go down. Next time you need a bigger hit to get the same rush, receptors go down. And then you need a bigger hit and a bigger hit and a bigger hit until finally you get a huge hit to get nothing. That's called tolerance.\"\n- \"I walked up to this concession in Cape Town with all these amazing cinnamon rolls... and I looked at them and there was zero part of my brain that was interested in any of it. Zero part of my brain. And I was like, 'Wow, my brain has been rewired or something just because I've removed sugar from my diet.'\" — Steven Bartlett\n- \"The food industry tells you, 'Well, carbohydrates are energy.' Actually, that's not true. Carbohydrates inhibit energy production.\"\n- \"If a substrate that passes your lips does not contribute to growth and does not contribute to burning, is it a food?... It's a poison.\"\n\n---\n\n### S-010 — Tony Cosentino Podcast Transcript\n\n**Key excerpts retained:**\n- \"I've been trying to give up sugar for years I've tried quitting and it'd last for about two weeks and then I'd start saying I can just have a little bit of something a little bit sugar and within an hour or two of having some sugar I was back into full blown sugar addiction.\"\n- \"I would spend pretty much all my pocket money on lollies my brother would save it. So he always had money and I always had no money because I was buying as much sugar as I could get with my pocket money.\"\n- \"Apparently also I had a baby I was given a sugar syrup kind of a drink to calm me down you know pacifiers sort of stuff that people used to use in those days.\"\n- \"Like third generation sugar addict I'd say I am because my grandfather... he got type 2 diabetes in his 50s.\"\n- \"I used to eat bags and bags of starbursts because it had kind of a fruity background flavour I could eat a couple bags a day of that when I was working.\"\n- \"If they'd only seen my rubbish bin where my work area was, it was full to the brim of lolly packets. Yeah it was such a terrible thing. I would hide that sugar consumption.\"\n- \"if I have something a bag of lollies I couldn't stop eating it till it was gone and then I'd still not feel satisfied and I'd feel worse probably after having the whole bag then when I started out. So it never used to quench my thirst for sugar.\"\n- \"By the third week the cravings were gone and I really couldn't care less about sugar. It was quite quite amazing how much the addiction stopped.\"\n- \"getting control of that part of my life made me feel like I can be in control. It's made me feel a lot better about myself and about going for bigger goals.\"\n- \"I lost about 10 kilos without changing exercise routines or normal food intake. Purely just taking sugar out of the equation.\"\n\n---\n\n### S-011 — PRX: \"Can a doughnut be a drug?\" (Jill & Eliza)\n\n**Key excerpts retained:**\n- \"I got the idea in my head last night that I wanted to have sugar, and bought some really gross sugar that I would normally never eat, and I bought like twice as much... I just made myself sick, and I wonder if it is ever going to end. I feel really hopeless right now about it, and I'm scared, actually.\" — Jill\n- \"I really just wanted to keep eating – I wanted to go back in the kitchen and eat all the yogurt I bought. I had this really crazy moment of just wishing I could go back to the store and get the cake, and just eat the whole cake…\" — Jill\n- \"I used to have fantasies that the only way I would be able to lose weight, and stop binging, would be to be put in jail.\" — Eliza\n- \"The white powder that you sniff up your nose or the white powder that you put in your throat – it alters your mood, it makes you a different person. It's definitely a drug.\" — Eliza\n- \"There's something about the repetitive motion in eating a lot of food that puts you in a place – it's kinda like you kind of leave your body a little bit. If anyone tries to interrupt me, like on the phone or at the door, I get really angry, because I do not want to be disturbed.\" — Eliza\n- \"After I binge, it takes about five days to get back to normal... if I feel suddenly uncomfortable, angry or moody, I don't know if that's how I really feel, or if it's because of the food. It plays with my emotions for about five days. That's a pretty big price to pay for a 20-minute binge.\" — Eliza\n\n---\n\n### S-012 — NPR: \"Curbing Chocolate\" (Joseph C. Phillips)\n\n**Key excerpts retained:**\n- \"I'll leap over my wife to get to a chocolate covered toffee bar. I'll wrestle my sons for peanut butter cups. Dark, white or milk chocolate-it makes no difference. I have to have it.\"\n- \"Late at night I even sneak through my sons' stashes, swiping all the good stuff, leaving them nothing but candy corn.\"\n- \"When it comes to sweets in general, and chocolate in particular, I have no self control.\"\n- \"I feel like a DEA agent in my own home. I've begun frisking my sons at the door and will soon begin random backpack searches.\"\n\n---\n\n### S-013 — Dr. Eric Berg: \"How to Reset Your Body in 14 Days\"\n\n**Key excerpts retained:**\n- \"Most people who try to quit sugar fail on day three to four. Because right here is the moment where your brain's reward system is at its lowest point. Exactly right before things will start getting better, people tend to quit.\"\n- \"Brain fog, being irritable, headaches, tired, anxiety, pressure, agitation, all of that comes from cortisol because of this dopamine situation right here. You are not giving in to it, so the body is going to try to get you to give in to it.\"\n- \"By day 14, you're going to have normal dopamine receptors. So your food's going to taste better. And if you did eat sugar, it's going to be like incredibly sweet, way way sweeter than it normally is.\"\n- \"So, the best thing you can do is start to change your environment. What am I talking about changing your environment? I'm talking about purging the junk food from your kitchen.\"\n\n---\n\n## PART 2: RAW-BANK LINES\n\n### BANK 1 — Justification Inventory (verbatim quotes, in-voice)\n\n```\n- [Bank 1] \"well, I did go to the gym today.\" — Persona IDs: P-01 — S-001#E-001 [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"Overall I eat pretty healthy.\" — Persona IDs: P-01 — S-001#E-001 [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"It's not like I do this every day.\"... Until I started to do it every day. — Persona IDs: P-01 — S-001#E-001 [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"I love sweets, I love dessert, big fan, and I don't want to just get rid of it completely, because I think in this life we need to actually enjoy things, but I want to bring it back in moderation.\" — Persona IDs: P-01, P-04 — S-001#E-004 [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"I've learned that honestly I love sugar way too much I really do have a sweet tooth... cutting Sugar by 80 okay okay that's a lot easier\" — Persona IDs: P-04 — S-002#E-003 [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"I used to eat healthy all day and then I'd always have a little sweet treat usually in the afternoon... It was my sweet treat and my coffee.\" — Persona IDs: P-01, P-03 — S-003#E-002 [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"I felt like I needed it for everything. So if work was busy, It would be so much better if I had some chocolate with me. If I'd had a bad day, then suddenly I'd find myself at the petrol station buying chocolate.\" — Persona IDs: P-17 — S-007 transcript [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"there was usually chocolate on special. So even if I didn't particularly like that brand I'd buy it cause it was cheap.\" — Persona IDs: P-17 — S-007 transcript [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"It was not about the event or the people. This was a great reason for me to be able to indulge in sugar in a socially acceptable way.\" — Persona IDs: P-17 — S-007 transcript [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"my son is coming from Canada... and he's bringing me Canadian chocolate bars. So, I can't say that I'm being 100% sugar-free, but after those chocolate bars are gone and he leaves, yes, I will be 100% sugarfree.\" — Persona IDs: P-15 — S-004#E-005 [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"When I'm sick, I crave junk food. Like, I want greasy burgers and fries and chips and chocolate bars. Like, I want all the shitty food... And I tried to resist the urge and I couldn't.\" — Persona IDs: P-17 — S-004#E-003 [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"I can just have a little bit of something a little bit sugar and within an hour or two of having some sugar I was back into full blown sugar addiction.\" — Persona IDs: P-02 — S-010 transcript [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"I'll leap over my wife to get to a chocolate covered toffee bar. I'll wrestle my sons for peanut butter cups... I have to have it.\" — Persona IDs: P-18 (comic-self-aware) — S-012 transcript [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"Late at night I even sneak through my sons' stashes, swiping all the good stuff, leaving them nothing but candy corn.\" — Persona IDs: P-18 — S-012 transcript [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"People made desserts just for me, and my whole identity was wrapped up in my love for sweet foods, desserts, chocolate, ice cream, whatever. Chocolate was my best friend.\" — Persona IDs: P-07 — S-016 (Netta Ep 217) [slot: justification-menu; INTERPRETATION based on show notes]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"I used to watch other people on social media talk about how they quit sugar, how their cravings went away, and how their taste buds changed. And I honestly thought they were lying.\" — Persona IDs: P-07 — S-003#E-001 [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"It's not about the taste. If it was, we would do that thing where you'd have a little sweet. You'd swizzle it around your mouth and then you'd spit it out. But nobody does that. We eat it.\" — Persona IDs: P-17 — S-007 transcript [slot: justification-menu]\n\n- [Bank 1] \"I don't ever use the word treat around food anymore. It seems extreme but for me it was really necessary because treat implies something that's going to be good for you and delicious.\" — Persona IDs: P-10 — S-007 transcript [slot: justification-menu]\n```\n\n### BANK 2 — Belief Map\n\n```\n- [Bank 2] \"I honestly thought they were lying. I thought there's no way they're telling the truth. But I'm here to tell you that it is true. It is fact.\" — Persona IDs: P-07 — S-003#E-001 — **BELIEF REVERSAL**: \"cravings can't really go away\" → \"they do\" [slot: belief-map; KEYSTONE-BELIEF adjacent]\n\n- [Bank 2] \"I did not know that by feeding this habit, it was actually keeping the cycle alive... It was keeping me stuck in this constant tired, fatigued cycle.\" — Persona IDs: P-03, P-08 — S-003#E-002 — **BELIEF REVERSAL**: \"the treat fixes my energy\" → \"the treat causes the crash\" [slot: belief-map; KEYSTONE-BELIEF]\n\n- [Bank 2] \"Quitting sugar was way harder than quitting smoking was. And that's no joke.\" — Persona IDs: P-14 — S-004#E-001 — **BELIEF SURFACE**: \"sugar isn't a real addiction\" → \"it's harder than nicotine\" [slot: belief-map]\n\n- [Bank 2] \"I would never pass up a slice of cake before, ever. So, that's very different to me.\" — Persona IDs: P-07, P-10 — S-003#E-004 — **IDENTITY SHIFT**: \"I'm a cake person\" → \"that's not who I am anymore\" [slot: belief-map]\n\n- [Bank 2] \"getting control of that part of my life made me feel like I can be in control.\" — Persona IDs: P-20 (control-seeker) — S-010 transcript — **BELIEF SHIFT**: \"I have no control\" → \"control is possible\" [slot: belief-map]\n\n- [Bank 2] \"I just realised it was like poison. It was just killing me.\" — Persona IDs: P-17 — S-007 transcript — **BELIEF TRANSFORMATION**: \"sugar is a pleasure\" → \"sugar is poison\" [slot: belief-map; KEYSTONE-BELIEF]\n\n- [Bank 2] \"I had this really crazy moment of just wishing I could go back to the store and get the cake, and just eat the whole cake…\" — Persona IDs: P-19 (loss-of-control) — S-011 transcript — **BELIEF**: \"I can stop when I want\" → evidence of complete loss of control [slot: belief-map]\n\n- [Bank 2] \"I used to have fantasies that the only way I would be able to lose weight, and stop binging, would be to be put in jail.\" — Persona IDs: P-19 — S-011 transcript — **BELIEF**: \"I should be able to control this with willpower\" → fantasy of external control [slot: belief-map]\n```\n\n### BANK 3 — Lived-Experience Bank\n\n```\n- [Bank 3] \"I had lost all self-control in the face of a free donut or plate of cookies.\" — Persona IDs: P-01 — S-001#E-001 [slot: sensory]\n\n- [Bank 3] \"instinctively I went to my snack cabinet and I'll show you guys what I found. That's it. Organic rice cake. Nothing, nothing sweet there.\" — Persona IDs: P-01, P-02 — S-001#E-002 [slot: sensory; inversion]\n\n- [Bank 3] \"No longer did I have huge swings of high to low energy throughout the day... So you go back up, you feel good for a little while, and then you crash again.\" — Persona IDs: P-01, P-03 — S-001#E-003 [slot: sensory]\n\n- [Bank 3] \"with day six and seven my energy levels absolutely crashed I mean I was so exhausted literally I couldn't even move and that's no exaggeration\" — Persona IDs: P-02, P-06 — S-002#E-001 [slot: sensory; withdrawal]\n\n- [Bank 3] \"in the second week that's when I really started to feel the most improvements... I started to feel much more energized I stopped to experience those kind of massive drops in energy in the afternoon\" — Persona IDs: P-02, P-03 — S-002#E-002 [slot: sensory; freedom-texture]\n\n- [Bank 3] \"I ate it and that whole rest of the day I felt terrible. My I had a tummy ache. It didn't even taste that great. It was so unbearably sweet to me.\" — Persona IDs: P-07, P-09 — S-003#E-003 [slot: sensory; special-moments]\n\n- [Bank 3] \"I did not lose a fraction of a pound by quitting sugar... Absolutely zero.\" — Persona IDs: P-11 — S-003#E-005 [slot: sensory; freedom-texture]\n\n- [Bank 3] \"I have no pain like all my pain is virtually gone... that pain is 98% gone... I have no pain in my my elbows, my wrists, my fingers, there's no pain there. My knees, everything is 98 99% pain-free.\" — Persona IDs: P-15, P-16 — S-004#E-002 [slot: sensory; freedom-texture]\n\n- [Bank 3] \"I was eating chocolate every day, as much as I could. Sort of get away with without people seeing.\" — Persona IDs: P-17 — S-007 transcript [slot: 