s, Bitten has developed methods that work. She explains why treating addiction must come first, before trauma work or therapy\n\n[...]\n\nBitten Johnson has been sober from alcohol for 39 years, but quitting sugar? That was the real battle.\n\n[...]\n\nWhether you're struggling with food cravings yourself or trying to understand why willpower isn't enough, this interview offers rare insights from someone who's walked the path and dedicated her life to lighting the way for others."},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://omny.fm/shows/a-really-good-cry/how-to-break-up-with-sugar-reboot-your-body-and-re","title":"How to Break Up with Sugar, Reboot Your Body and Reduce Cravings - A Really Good Cry - Omny.fm","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"In this episode of A Really Good Cry, I share my personal journey of overcoming sugar cravings and embracing a more balanced, fulfilling life. From the shocking reality of how much sugar we consume daily to the emotional and physical grip it has on us, I dive into the effects of sugar on our bodies and minds.\n\n[...]\n\n- 00:00 Intro\n- 01:16 How I started a sugar detox\n- 07:12 Benefits of a sugar detox\n- 09:17 “Do not wait to feel different before you make a change in your life”\n-\n\n[...]\n\nWhether you're looking for a full sugar detox or just trying to cut back, this episode will inspire and equip you to take control of your cravings—one day at a time. Let's reset, rebalance\n\n[...]\n\n10:08 The shocking truth about sugar consumption\n- 11:40 Plan how you’re giving up sugar\n- 13:37 Find alternatives to sugar\n- 14:36 Check the labels of the food you eat\n- 16:06 Plan for the scenarios you struggle to resist\n- 16:50 Increase your protein intake\n- 18:23 Difference between being full and feeling satiated\n- 19:15 Don’t skip meals\n-\n\n[...]\n\nand create healthier habits together!\n\n[...]\n\n20:05 Drink water and mind your business\n\n[...]\n\n20:53 How sleep is related to obesity\n\n[...]\n\never thought about how