said no. No. No. No. No way.\n\nSo what changed?\n\nListen to this episode to hear how and why I ended up trying something that that I'd never tried before and that seemed crazy, and what made living sugar free so much easier.\n\n[...]\n\n\"THIS made living sugar free so much easier!\": Netta (Episode 217) - Life After Sugar Podcast\n\n# Listen to episode 217:\n\n[...]\n\nthat\n\n[...]\n\n!\n\n[...]\n\nfeel in control around\n\n[...]\n\ncan slim down"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://podcast.aftersugarclub.com/episode-219/","title":"\"My health was transformed when I cut gluten and sugar\": Colleen (Episode 219) - Life After Sugar Podcast","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"Listen to Colleen's inspiring story of how cutting gluten and sugar transformed her health - and her life!\n\n[...]\n\nAnd to her amazement, after just two weeks, her chronic symptoms faded, she came off nearly all medications, and for the first time in years, she had the energy to truly live.\n\n[...]\n\nShe overhauled her diet, including cutting gluten and sugar.\n\n[...]\n\nBack in her 20s, Colleen was suffering from chronic exhaustion, pain, and bloating. She was unable to function and she was sleeping all the time.\n\n[...]\n\nThen Colleen discovered functional nutrition, and she tried something she had never tried before.\n\n[...]\n\n\"My health was transformed when I cut gluten and sugar\": Colleen (Episode 219) - Life After Sugar Podcast\n\n[...]\n\nDespite taking a cocktail of medications, nothing seemed to work.\n\n[...]\n\n# \"My health was transformed when I cut gluten and sugar\": Colleen\n\n[...]\n\nMarch 23, 2025\n\n[...]\n\n# Listen to episode 219:\n\n[...]\n\nof"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://podcast.nettagorman.com/episode-175/","title":"\"Now I feel free from the hold sugar had on me\": Danielle (Episode 175) - Life After Sugar Podcast","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"Listen to Danielle describe her slow 3-year process to finally feel free from the hold sugar had on her.\n\n[...]\n\nDanielle's journey with sugar started in childhood. She remembers that sugar was a massive part of her upbringing.\n\n[...]\n\nDanielle says that sugar was the coping and addictive mechanisms that had been handed down through her family line. Her mom, she explains, was someone who never felt emotions, and she used food to numb and escape. So Danielle got that pattern from her.\n\nBut then in her late twenties, Danielle started looking more deeply into her early childhood traumas and what contributed to the addictive patterning in her brain.And that was the start of an awakening for her.\n\n[...]\n\nSo there was a lot of rewarding with sugar.As a child, Danielle was an extremely picky eater. She ate lots of carbs, like white pasta and rice cakes... which, she says, no doubt really put her on a blood sugar roller coaster at a very young age.\n\n[...]\n\nWith her family, she always had ice cream after dinner. Sugar was always a treat.They even had a trunk in their house that had little goodie bags with sweet treats for whenever she and her brother were good.\n\n[...]\n\n\"Now I feel free from the hold sugar had on me\": Danielle (Episode 175) - Life After Sugar Podcast\n\n# Listen to episode 175:\n\n# \"Now I feel free from the hold sugar had on me\": Danielle\n\nMay 19, 2024\n\n[...]\n\nrid of cravings so that you can slim down and finally feel in control around food!"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://podcast.aftersugarclub.com/episode-198/","title":"\"I don't numb the pain away with sugar anymore\": Sarah (Episode 198) - Life After Sugar Podcast","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"So she went on a 30-day elimination diet where she cut out categories of foods, like legumes and dairy and grains and certain fruits, certain starchy vegetables... and of course, sugar. Later, she also cut alcohol.\n\n[...]\n\n\"I don't numb the pain away with sugar anymore\": Sarah (Episode 198) - Life After Sugar Podcast\n\n[...]\n\nUntil her late thirties, when she decided to do a popular elimination diet. She had no weight to lose at the time, but she wanted to see what the hype was about.\n\n[...]\n\nBut that 30-day elimination diet put Sarah in a calorie restricted state. And for the first time in her life, she felt totally out of control around food.\n\nListen to how cutting sugar and alcohol forced Sarah to learn to deal with her emotional pain and physical pain in healthier ways. And how she developed healthier coping skills than sugar or food.\n\n[...]\n\nSarah grew up with a mother who was very intentional with feeding her family healthy food. She cooked everything from scratch.\n\nAs a child, Sarah didn't have any exposure to sugar whatsoever.\n\nAnd because there was no option for sugar in her life, Sarah says that she was neutral around food.\n\n[...]\n\n# Listen to episode 198:\n\n# \"I don't numb the pain away with sugar anymore\": Sarah\n\nOctober 27, 2024\n\n[...]\n\naround food!\n\n[...]\n\ndown and finally feel in\n\n[...]\n\nthat you\n\n[...]\n\nof"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://podcast.aftersugarclub.com/episode-224/","title":"\"Cutting dairy and sugar gave me back my health\": Mark (Episode 224) - Life After Sugar Podcast","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"When Mark started eating low carb and reduced added sugar, his candida symptoms went away too.\n\n[...]\n\nMark was experiencing inflammatory bowel syndrome (IBS) and asthma, and when he cut dairy from his diet, his symptoms disappeared.\n\n[...]\n\n\"Cutting dairy and sugar gave me back my health\": Mark (Episode 224) - Life After Sugar Podcast\n\n[...]\n\nMark and I are both big fans of questioning and experimenting.\n\n[...]\n\nMark's health issues started early in his teenage years. Growing up in the north east of the UK, he'd been put on antibiotics for an ear infection, and at the age of 16 his doctor wanted to put him on anti-depressants.\n\n[...]\n\nBut instead, Mark decided to study in the health field, which included changing his diet. And he started cooking for himself and experimenting with different foods.\n\n[...]\n\nAnd I hope that this thought-provoking episode will inspire you to start making changes that work for YOU.\n\n[...]\n\n# \"Cutting dairy and sugar gave me back my health\": Mark\n\n[...]\n\nApril 27, 2025\n\n[...]\n\nof\n\n[...]\n\n# Listen to episode 224:"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://thisnakedmind.com/ep-269-breaking-up-with-sugar-with-molly-carmel/","title":"EP 269: Breaking Up with Sugar with Molly Carmel","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"# EP 269: Breaking Up with Sugar with Molly Carmel\n\nOn today’s episode, Annie Grace talks with fellow brain science lover Molly Carmel, an eating disorders and addictions therapist and author of Breaking Up with Sugar. Molly shares her story – from the beginning of her relationship with sugar in response to a childhood trauma to their breakup over 10 years ago – including how Molly ate her way through bariatric surgery and ultimately got rid of dieting, changed her relationship with food, and lost 175 pounds.\n\n[...]\n\nEP 269: Breaking Up with Sugar with Molly Carmel - This Naked Mind\n\n[...]\n\nDownload Transcript\n\n[...]\n\nRelated Episodes\n\n[...]\n\nHave you tried The Alcohol Experiment\n\n[...]\n\nOkay, if not, drop everything and go to thisnakedmind.com/experiment. This free 30-day challenge is designed\n\n[...]\n\ninterrupt your patterns and put you back in touch with the best version of you. You remember, it was that version of you that’s living your most joyful life, the version that doesn’t need alcohol to relax\n\n[...]\n\nAnnie Grace"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://thehealthinvestment.com/sugar/","title":"How To Break Up With Sugar & Find Food Freedom | Molly Carmel","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"**MINUTE-BY-MINUTE BREAKDOWN OF THE EPISODE:**\n* 2:52 – Molly Carmel’s history of addiction and obesity\n* 14:43 – Is*everyone*addicted to sugar?\n* 17:52 – Wha