aples, wellness picks & more:\nhttps://www.shopltk.com/explore/Anna_Saccone\n\n⸻\n\n💬 If you enjoyed this video, don’t forget to LIKE + COMMENT…it really helps more people see it! And if you’re new here, I’d love to have you subscribe 🥰\n\n♥ SUBSCRIBE for weekly videos on beauty, wellness + mum life:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/c/AnnaSaccone?sub_confirmation=1\n\n⸻\n\n📱 COME SAY HI\nTikTok: https://www.tiktok.com/@annasaccone\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/annasaccone\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/TheStyleDiet\n\n⸻\n\n📌 DISCLAIMER\nThis video is for educational/informational purposes only and not intended to diagnose or treat any medical condition. Always consult a qualified healthcare provider for personal advice.\n\n⸻\n\n#quittingsugar #sugarfreejourney #beautyfromwithin #annasaccone #nutritionstudent #momof4life #glowupfromtheinside #hormonehealth\n\n## Transcript\n\nI'm styling my hair this morning and I wanted to chat to you guys about something that has made a huge difference in my life recently and that is quitting sugar. For those of you that are new here, my name is Anna. I'm a 37year-old mom of four and I have gone back to school to be a nutritionist.\nI've also had my own fair share of struggles with food and body image. I struggled for 15 years and recovered six years ago fully. So, I'm really proud of that. And on that note, I just wanted to put a quick disclaimer at the start of this video. If you are struggling with the same kind of thing right now, or if you are in recovery, you might want to consider skipping this video. I feel a real sense of responsibility, and I never want to put out any information that is not safe. I personally had to go allin with my recovery and I would never recommend this sort of thing to anyone who was not at a really good place with food and body image. I feel like it's just a place that you need to get to before you can make changes like the ones that I'm going to be talking about in this video. Firstly, let's 